// CBOR for `core.Value`.
//
// One codec, not two. JSON lives in `core` — `Value::to_json` and
// `Value::from_json` are the `$`-tagged spelling — because a value's JSON is
// something the whole framework writes and reads, not something a wasm format
// invented. CBOR is here because it is the FORMAT's encoding: the faithful one,
// where every arm survives and a value that cannot be encoded is an error
// rather than a silent null.
//
// The split is the two jobs. JSON is what an agent writes by hand and a browser
// parses without a library, and it is lossy on the way back in (a plain number
// is a double). CBOR is what a value crosses a process boundary as, and it is
// not.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/core" @tutuca,
  "moonbitlang/x/encoding",
  "moonbitlang/core/set",
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
}
